To build Openbox from git you need:

- A C Compiler (GCC or Clang)
- Meson 1.10+
- Ninja
- pkg-config
- GNU Gettext (optional, for translations)
- Xlib 1.8+ library/headers (devel package)
- Xau 1.0.11+ library/headers (devel package)
- GLib 2.88+ library/headers (devel package) (http://www.gtk.org)
- libxml2 2.12+ library/headers (devel package)
- Pango 1.57+ and PangoXft library/headers (devel package)
- Xft 2.3.6+ library/headers (devel package)

Also you will probably want:
- Imlib2 1.12+ library/headers (devel package)
- librsvg 2.61+ library/headers (devel package)
- X Cursor 1.2+ library/headers (devel package)
- Startup Notification 0.12+ library/headers (devel package)
- X11 Session Management (libSM 1.2+ / libICE 1.1+) library/headers (devel package)
- X11 extensions: XKB, XRandR 1.5+, XShape (Xext 1.3+), Xinerama 1.1+, XSync (Xext 1.3+)

We recommend the latest versions of all these packages.

Do the following to build and install Openbox from git:

% meson setup build
% meson compile -C build
% meson test -C build
% sudo meson install -C build

See `meson configure` (or `meson.options`) for available build options.

Don't try running it from the build directory without installing, it won't
work. It needs to be installed before it is run.

The following commands will be available: openbox-session,
  openbox-gnome-session, openbox-kde-session, and openbox.

See the man pages for details about them.  If you want to run Openbox on its
  own, you probably want to run "openbox-session".



----
In Ubuntu/Debian, you want these packages:

gcc
meson
ninja-build
gettext
pkg-config
libpango1.0-dev
libglib2.0-dev
libxml2-dev
libstartup-notification0-dev
xorg-dev
libimlib2-dev
librsvg2-dev

----
